{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774955568,"nonce":"CZSYcxqz4x/GxGiTzAPFikUgFqQ=","title":"Support alternative LLM providers via ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL passthrough and per-issue workflow override","message":"Enable nightshift to run on Anthropic-compatible LLM providers (e.g., MiniMax M2.7 at api.minimax.io/anthropic) alongside Claude.\n\n## Phase 1: Per-issue override (implement now)\n\n### Fix 1: Pass ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL to container\nAdd \"ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\" to _PASSTHROUGH_ENV_VARS in host/docker_cmd.py. Currently only ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is passed — the base URL is missing, so containers can't reach alternative providers.\n\n### Usage\nCreate a separate workflow file (e.g., WORKFLOW-m27.md) with:\n```yaml\nagent:\n  kind: claude-code\n  extra_args: [\"--model\", \"m2.7\"]\n```\n\nAnd a project .env with:\n```\nANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.minimax.io/anthropic\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-minimax-key\n```\n\nLaunch with: `nightshift start \u003cissue-id\u003e --workflow WORKFLOW-m27.md`\n\n### Scope\n- One-line change in host/docker_cmd.py (_PASSTHROUGH_ENV_VARS)\n- Update tests if _PASSTHROUGH_ENV_VARS is validated anywhere\n\n## Phase 2: Automatic fallback (future, document only)\n\nTwo complementary features for automatic overflow to alternative providers:\n\n### Fallback chain in config\nWORKFLOW.md declares primary + fallback provider:\n```yaml\nagent:\n  kind: claude-code\n  max_turns: 50\n  fallback:\n    extra_args: [\"--model\", \"m2.7\"]\n    env:\n      ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL: https://api.minimax.io/anthropic\n      ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: $MINIMAX_API_KEY\n```\n\n### Auth-failure triggers provider swap\nExtend the watcher's existing check_auth_failures() path: after N retries on the primary provider, swap env vars to the fallback provider and retry. No new detection logic needed — auth-failure detection already exists (AgentEventType.AUTH_FAILURE, suspended:auth-failure, MAX_AUTH_RETRIES).\n\nThe fallback_env section in WORKFLOW.md provides the alternative credentials. The watcher injects them when relaunching the container after primary provider exhaustion.\n\nPhase 2 should be filed as a separate issue when ready to implement.\n\nREQ: REQ-001 (agent lifecycle). Phase 2 needs new REQ for multi-provider support.","files":null}]}